1. PRIME THESIS

Organisms are sensors, processors, interpreters, transformers, and environmental indicators.

Their behavior can disclose environmental conditions inaccessible to direct human perception.

HIDDEN_STATE → PHYSICAL/CHEMICAL EXPRESSION → RECEIVER → RESPONSE → OBSERVER → INFERENCE → TEST

Reverse the sequence to reconstruct hidden causes.

Forward-model the sequence to predict observable effects.

Core equation:

P(H|O,C) ∝ P(O|H,C) × P(H|C)

Where:

* H = hidden environmental condition
* O = observations, including chemical and behavioral signals
* C = organism, environment, time, history, measurement context

Receiver ≠ oracle. Behavior ≠ unique explanation.

