10. PLAYBOOKS / DISCOVERY PROTOCOLS

P1 ANT_HIGHWAY

Observe → map traffic → identify branches/endpoints → inspect vegetation, aphids, nectaries, fruit, nesting → record conditions → revisit → compare explanations.

No baiting or destruction required. Do not infer human edibility.

P2 PLANT_VOLATILES

Compare undamaged, mechanically damaged, and herbivore-attacked plants; control species, developmental stage, environment, and timing.

Measure volatiles using validated GC-MS methods when laboratory access exists. Use authentic standards, blanks, replication, and detection limits.

P3 RHIZOSPHERE

Map host plants, fungi, soil conditions, root exudates, and microbial associations; test against moisture, soil chemistry, seasonality, and host-genotype confounders.

P4 SPIDER_WEB_E_DNA

Passive environmental sampling → contamination controls → laboratory DNA extraction/sequencing → species hypotheses → independent confirmation.

Detection does not establish exact current animal location.

P5 TERMITE_COMPARATIVE_MORPHOLOGY

Use scientific literature, microbiome data, metabolic maps, and mass-balance models to distinguish host functions from symbiont functions.

11. EVIDENCE GOVERNANCE

Evidence ladder:

E0: observation only
E1: association
E2: demonstrated mechanism
E3: controlled causal evidence
E4: independent replication/generalization
E5: externally validated, calibrated translation

Every claim retains:

claim_id, organism_scope, mechanism, source, DOI, methods, controls, environment, time, sample_size, uncertainty, rival_hypotheses, confidence_type, version, failure_modes

Do not silently replace original observations with later interpretations.

Preserve both occurrence time and analysis/entry time.

Failure operators

FALSE_CENTER: one observed behavior, multiple plausible causes.

FALSE_SYNTAX: one chemical interpreted as a universal word.

FALSE_CAUSATION: correlation promoted without intervention or controls.

FALSE_PRECISION: uncalibrated outputs presented as empirical confidence.

FALSE_TRANSFER: biological analogy treated as a proven engineering solution.

Repairs must preserve counterexamples and the tests that resolved them.

